From 71104ec9c55c7578cc50c2e25d3e2254304c5a67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:56:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a library listing be narrowed to one first letter

A big library is only reachable by scrolling. The listing pages 50 items at a
time, so reaching T in a few thousand artists is dozens of round-trips, and the
search box does not help: it matches anywhere in the name, so "t" returns every
item containing one.

library_items gains starts_with: a single letter, or "#" for the items filed
under no letter at all. Two details make it behave rather than merely work.

It filters on whichever name column the current ordering sorts on, so the items
kept are the ones that really appear under that letter - sorted by sort name,
"The Beatles" is under B, and filtering on search_name would have hidden it from
the letter the list files it under.

It is a range rather than LIKE 'x%', so SQLite seeks into the index that is
already there:

  SEARCH artists USING INDEX artists_search_sort_name_idx
    (search_sort_name>? AND search_sort_name<?)

That also makes it cheaper than the contains-search it sits beside. The columns
are already lowercase and diacritic-folded, so Atna files under A and the '#'
bucket is simply everything sorting below 'a' - digits, and the empty string a
name like '!!!' reduces to.

